{"kind":"article","topicSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Operators","title":"Operators","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLEnding\/!=(_:_:)"]}],"sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlending\/equatable-implementations"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLEnding\/Equatable-Implementations","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"role":"collectionGroup","title":"Equatable Implementations","roleHeading":"API Collection"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLEnding"]]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLEnding":{"type":"topic","title":"MXLEnding","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLEnding","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The ending type represents multiple (e.g. first and second) endings. Typically, the start type is associated"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with the left barline of the first measure in an ending. The stop and discontinue types are associated with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the right barline of the last measure in an ending. Stop is used when the ending mark concludes with a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"downward jog, as is typical for first endings. Discontinue is used when there is no downward jog, as is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"typical for second endings that do not conclude a piece. The length of the jog can be specified using the end-"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"length attribute. The text-x and text-y attributes are offsets that specify where the baseline of the start of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the ending text appears, relative to the start of the ending line."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLEnding"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLEnding"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlending"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLEnding/!=(_:_:)":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[],"title":"!=(_:_:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLEnding\/!=(_:_:)","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlending\/!=(_:_:)","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"!=","kind":"identifier"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]}}}